IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `as65-nouns`

-- Row il-65. THE TWO ITEMS (I1 and I2), as typed values, each with a sound control beside it.
-- The Act in Sefer HaChukim 3510 (31 March 2026) is called "the Act" below. Its s 31 amends the Assurance Law. The row says what each instrument prints and what the row records.
-- ITEM I1: a definition that the Act inserts into s 1 of the Assurance Law prints a defined term, and cites s 36ט of the Banking (Licensing) Law, 5741-1981 for it by a shorter name than the one the consolidation of the Banking Law prints in s 36ט.
-- ITEM I2: an instruction of the Act replaces one string in subsection (ב) of s 3ג2 of the Assurance Law, in every place; in paragraph (2) of the subsection the string stands at one place exactly and a prefixed spelling of it at another, in the earlier revision of the consolidation.
-- CONTROLS: for I1, item (6) of s 31 of the Act cites s 3ג2 of the Assurance Law, and the consolidation prints a heading for s 3ג2; for I2, the chapeau of (ב) and paragraphs (1) and (3), where the string stands exactly in the earlier revision and the replacing words stand in the current one.
-- Each reading says where it was read from (see `Where a reading comes from` in as65-nouns.l4). The Hebrew Wikisource text is not official, and anything resting only on it is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY.
-- The row states no commencement day and says nothing about whether any provision of the Act is in force. It does not say that the Law or anyone is wrong, and it does not say what a court would do with the words.
-- The printed pages show a section number such as 3ג2 with its last digit as a small raised numeral; this file types it as a plain digit, as the consolidation does. ASCII quotation marks stand for the printed ones.
-- The consolidation of the Assurance Law is the Hebrew Wikisource page whose title line, in the current revision, is line 2 of the excerpt of that revision.

§ `I1: the definition that cites s 36ט of the Banking (Licensing) Law`

-- The citing words, as the Act prints them: read from the deposited cropped images of the pages printed 365 and 366 (PDF pages 17 and 18).
-- The page printed 365 holds the heading of s 31, with its margin note, and the first item of s 31, which inserts definitions into s 1 of the Assurance Law; the page printed 366 holds one of the inserted definitions. The lines of the page printed 365 after the words shown, and the lines of the page printed 366 before the definition, are not deposited and are not read here.
-- The definition stands between the opening words of item (1), at the foot of the page printed 365, and item (2), on the page printed 366; that it belongs to item (1) rests on that order, and the lines between are not deposited.
