§ `Counting the places`

GIVEN i IS A `An instruction that replaces words`
      ps IS A LIST OF `A place that holds words`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many of the places hold the replaced string exactly in revision 2968704` MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `the words at the place in revision 2968704` EQUALS i's `the string the instruction replaces`) ps)

GIVEN i IS A `An instruction that replaces words`
      ps IS A LIST OF `A place that holds words`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many of the places hold the replacing words in revision 3085793` MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `the words at the place in revision 3085793` EQUALS i's `the words the instruction puts in its place`) ps)

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `A place that holds words`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many of the places spell the words exactly in revision 2968704` MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `how the place spells the words in revision 2968704` EQUALS `exactly as the instruction names them`) ps)

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `A place that holds words`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many of the places spell the words with a prefix in revision 2968704` MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `how the place spells the words in revision 2968704` EQUALS `as the instruction names them, with a one-letter prefix on the first word and on the last`) ps)

GIVEN i IS A `An instruction that replaces words`
      ps IS A LIST OF `A place that holds words`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the replaced string stands at every one of the places` MEANS
    `how many of the places hold the replaced string exactly in revision 2968704` i ps EQUALS count ps

GIVEN i IS A `An instruction that replaces words`
      ps IS A LIST OF `A place that holds words`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the replacing words stand at every one of the places` MEANS
    `how many of the places hold the replacing words in revision 3085793` i ps EQUALS count ps

§ `Cross-references`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the target prints the name the citing words print` MEANS c's `the name as the citing words print it` EQUALS c's `the name as the target prints it`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the target has everything the citing words name` MEANS c's `how many of them the target has under that name` AT LEAST c's `how many things the citing words name`
